|~ qlang operand catalog — predicate family. Subject-first
   boolean operators (`eq`, logical combinators `and`/`or`/`not`); the
   ordering family `gt`/`lt`/`gte`/`lte` resides on the kinds it
   compares under its contracts in `core/lib/qlang/any.qlang`. The shape stays uniform:
   each fires per-call as a pure value test answering a boolean, the
   condition the higher-order `filter` / `every` / `any` / `if` /
   `cond` chain composes over [D14]. The identity-tag reader `type` and the `keyword`
   involution ride parallel axes and live in
   `core/lib/qlang/operand/typeClassifier.qlang` and
   `core/lib/qlang/operand/typeConversion.qlang` respectively. ~|

:not
  |~~ Logical negation of a boolean. Null is tested with `eq null`,
      and a subject of another kind is refused.

      ~(false | not | eq true)
      ~(true | not | eq false)
      ~(null | eq null | eq true)
  ~~|
  ::builtin{:impl :qlang/prim/not
            :category :predicate
            :subject :boolean
            :returns :boolean
   }

::NotSubjectNotBooleanError
  |~~ Subject of `not` must be a boolean.
      ~(
        0 | not
        !| [type /actualType]
        |  eq [::NotSubjectNotBooleanError ::number]
       )
  ~~|

:eq
  |~~ Returns true if the subject equals the captured value by
      structural equality (deep recursive comparison across Maps,
      Vecs, Sets, and scalars).

      ~(42 | eq 42 | eq true)
      ~({:a 1} | eq {:a 1} | eq true)
  ~~|
  ::builtin{:impl :qlang/prim/eq
            :category :predicate
            :subject :any
            :returns :boolean
            :modifiers [:any]
   }

:and
  |~~ Conjunction across captured sub-pipelines: each fires
      against pipeValue and answers a boolean, and both must be
      true. Use inside `filter` / `every` / `if` to compose
      multi-clause predicates over a single subject.

      ~({:active true :age 25} | and /active (/age | gte 18) | eq true)
      ~({:active false :age 25} | and /active (/age | gte 18) | eq false)
  ~~|
  ::builtin{:impl :qlang/prim/and
            :category :predicate
            :subject :any
            :returns :boolean
            :modifiers [:any]
   }

::AndLeftNotBooleanError
  |~~ The left condition of `and` must answer a boolean.
      ~(
        1 | and true
        !| [type /actualType]
        |  eq [::AndLeftNotBooleanError ::number]
       )
  ~~|

::AndRightNotBooleanError
  |~~ The right condition of `and` must answer a boolean.
      ~(
        true | and 1
        !| [type /actualType]
        |  eq [::AndRightNotBooleanError ::number]
       )
  ~~|

:or
  |~~ Disjunction across captured sub-pipelines: each fires
      against pipeValue and answers a boolean, and at least one
      must be true.

      ~(5  | or (eq 5) (eq 10) | eq true)
      ~(7  | or (eq 5) (eq 10) | eq false)
      ~({:role "admin"} | or (/role | eq "admin") (/role | eq "owner") | eq true)
  ~~|
  ::builtin{:impl :qlang/prim/or
            :category :predicate
            :subject :any
            :returns :boolean
            :modifiers [:any]
   }

::OrLeftNotBooleanError
  |~~ The left condition of `or` must answer a boolean.
      ~(
        1 | or true
        !| [type /actualType]
        |  eq [::OrLeftNotBooleanError ::number]
       )
  ~~|

::OrRightNotBooleanError
  |~~ The right condition of `or` must answer a boolean.
      ~(
        false | or 1
        !| [type /actualType]
        |  eq [::OrRightNotBooleanError ::number]
       )
  ~~|
